# faderbank: the DB8E shows the fader you just moved (issue #22, Group B).
# Spec: faderbank.md "Display" — it "automatically updates the display whenever
# you move one of the faders". The title is the moved lane's own `outputN`
# target, per the rule fadermatrix.md states for the bank family.
#
#   lane 1 -> O1        -> header "Output O1"
#   lane 2 -> _LEVEL    -> header "LEVEL"
#   lane 3 -> O3        -> header "Output O3"
#
# The last section pins the tie-break: the DB8E has ONE screen, so when several
# lanes change on the same tick the lowest-numbered one lands and the others
# stay pending (delay-not-discard, the same rule a rejected write follows) and
# land on the following tick. A hand moves one fader at a time; a tie only
# comes from a preset recall or, as here, a scripted input.
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[db8e]

[faderbank]
    firstfader = 1
    output1    = O1
    output2    = _LEVEL
    output3    = O3

[mixer]
    input1 = _LEVEL
    output = O8
>>>
@0 expectdisplay D1 off
@1 move F1 0.3
@1 expectdisplay D1 value 0.3 tol 1e-5
@1 expectdisplay D1 header "Output O1"
@2 expectdisplay D1 value 0.3 tol 1e-5
# A different fader: the screen switches, value and title together.
@3 move F2 0.8
@3 expectdisplay D1 value 0.8 tol 1e-5
@3 expectdisplay D1 header "LEVEL"
@4 move F3 0.25
@4 expectdisplay D1 value 0.25 tol 1e-5
@4 expectdisplay D1 header "Output O3"
# Two faders on one tick: lane 1 lands now, lane 2 is pending.
@5 move F1 0.6
@5 move F2 0.1
@5 expectdisplay D1 value 0.6 tol 1e-5
@5 expectdisplay D1 header "Output O1"
# ... and lands on the next tick rather than being dropped.
@6 expectdisplay D1 value 0.1 tol 1e-5
@6 expectdisplay D1 header "LEVEL"
